{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"45246929f529e7885396de70717efbc89f97997c7ce2402f0e6a9404661ebb05","digest":{"component_or_area":"Status mapping tests","key_entities":["_DRIFT_WARNED","resolve_outbound_status","reset_drift_warnings()","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py","test_drift_warning_deduped_within_pass","test_unmapped_status_drifts"],"problem_keywords":["test isolation","autouse fixture","process-global state","test ordering","drift warning deduplication"],"propositions":["Process-global _DRIFT_WARNED set in outbound_mapper suppresses duplicate drift warnings, causing test pollution under reordering when an earlier test populates the set before a later test asserts the warning is emitted.","Status-mapping tests lack per-test state reset, making test_unmapped_status_drifts brittle: if blocked status is recorded in _DRIFT_WARNED by a prior test, the stderr warning assertion fails.","Adding an autouse pytest fixture that calls outbound_mapper.reset_drift_warnings() before each test in the module ensures every test starts with an empty _DRIFT_WARNED and makes drift assertions order-independent.","The fixture reuses the existing public reset_drift_warnings() entry point rather than directly manipulating the private _DRIFT_WARNED set."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787903997604295001,"uuid":"120db1a4-bfbe-46a4-9999-d245f5868ed6"}